'''PYRAMID30 Abyala, S.A.''' is a [[Balboa]]n {{w|music chart}} and data compilation company and the Abyalan regional subsidiary of [[PYRAMID30 Inc.]], the Sanese music statistics corporation. Headquartered in [[Sant Cristòfor]], the company compiles and publishes music chart data across the [[Abyala]]n region, including domestic music charts for [[Balboa]], [[Balisca]], [[Potocsí]], [[Asikyira]], and [[Tapuya]]. It is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker P30.

== History ==

=== Música d'Abyala MDT (1973–2019) ===

The company was originally founded in 1973 as '''Música d'Abyala MDT''', a Sant Cristòfor-based music magazine that published news, reviews, and chart data covering the Abyalan music industry. MDT (standing for ''Música, Dades, Traça'', "Music, Data, Tracking") was established by a group of Balboan music journalists and radio broadcasters in the aftermath of [[Balboa]]n reunification, when the opening of the Abyalan music market created demand for a regional music publication that could track trends across multiple countries.

Initially published as a weekly print magazine, Música d'Abyala MDT compiled its chart data from radio airplay reports and retail sales surveys submitted by partner stores across the region. The magazine's flagship product was the '''Top 100 Abyala''' chart, a weekly top 100 singles ranking that combined physical sales and radio airplay data from across the Abyalan region. The Top 100 Abyala chart became the standard music chart for the region and was widely cited by radio stations, record labels, and media outlets across the five countries. The magazine also published domestic top 100 charts for individual markets, including the Top 100 Balboa, Top 100 Balisca, Top 100 Potocsí, Top 100 Asikyira, and Top 100 Tapuya.

As the music industry shifted from physical to digital consumption in the 2000s, Música d'Abyala MDT expanded its data collection to include digital download sales and, later, streaming metrics. The magazine transitioned from print to digital publication in the early 2010s, while its chart compilation business became the company's primary revenue source. However, the collapse of physical music sales across the Abyalan region in the 2010s eroded the company's core revenue base. Retail partners that had provided sales data reduced their orders or closed, and the company's print advertising revenue declined as the magazine shifted to digital. By 2018, Música d'Abyala MDT was operating at a loss, with declining revenue from its retail data contracts and insufficient digital subscription revenue to offset the decline.

=== Acquisition by PYRAMID30 (2019) ===

In 2019, [[PYRAMID30 Inc.]] acquired Música d'Abyala MDT for approximately $12 million as part of its international expansion strategy, following the parent company's success in establishing standardised music metrics across [[Okaiken]], [[Nakamizu]], and [[Yanbaru]]. The acquisition was motivated by Música d'Abyala MDT's existing data collection infrastructure and market relationships across the five Abyalan countries, which provided PYRAMID30 with an established regional presence rather than building from scratch. The purchase price reflected the company's distressed financial position — its data contracts, brand recognition, and regional footprint were worth more than its declining revenue stream.

Following the acquisition, the company was rebranded as PYRAMID30 Abyala, S.A. and integrated into the PYRAMID30 corporate structure. The existing Música d'Abyala MDT staff and data collection partnerships were retained, and the company adopted PYRAMID30's unified methodology, which added streaming metrics to the existing physical sales, digital downloads, and radio airplay data. The Top 100 Abyala chart and the domestic Top 100 charts were retained and continued to be published alongside the new PYRAMID30-branded top 30 charts.

== Charts ==

=== Regional charts ===

PYRAMID30 Abyala publishes the following regional charts for the Abyalan market:

* '''Top 100 Abyala''' — the regional top 100 singles chart, combining physical sales, digital downloads, streaming, and radio airplay data across all five markets, published weekly on Tuesdays (originally published by Música d'Abyala MDT since 2003)
* '''PYRAMID30 Abyala Singles Chart''' — the regional top 30 singles chart, using the PYRAMID30 methodology introduced in 2019
* '''PYRAMID30 Abyala Albums Chart''' — the regional top 30 albums chart
* '''PYRAMID30 Abyala Streaming Chart''' — streaming-only singles and albums rankings
* '''PYRAMID30 Abyala Airplay Chart''' — radio airplay rankings aggregated from partner stations across the five markets

=== Domestic charts ===

In addition to the regional charts, PYRAMID30 Abyala publishes domestic charts for each of its five markets. The Top 100 domestic charts were originally introduced by Música d'Abyala MDT and have been published continuously since the company's founding. The PYRAMID30-branded top 30 charts were introduced following the 2019 acquisition.

